WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.290
OPENING

00:18.580 --> 00:20.780
You know more than I thought.

00:20.780 --> 00:23.590
I thought you were just ignorant.

00:23.590 --> 00:24.880
Shut up!

00:25.220 --> 00:27.160
Never mind that, Gonza.

00:27.160 --> 00:31.860
Use whatever means you can find to get the
word out to Revinus across the nation!

00:31.860 --> 00:33.020
Word?

00:33.330 --> 00:36.060
Just one line: "Satsuma will rise."

00:36.060 --> 00:37.700
Satsuma will rise?!

00:37.700 --> 00:43.470
That's right. If they hear Satsuma will rise, there
will be those that will rise throughout the land.

00:43.470 --> 00:46.440
We will utilize the news censorship.

00:46.440 --> 00:48.680
They won't know if it's true or false.

00:48.680 --> 00:50.550
You're sending out false information?

00:50.550 --> 00:52.380
It's not false.

00:52.380 --> 00:55.320
That's what I'm really going to do.

01:07.800 --> 01:09.560
Sorry to keep you waiting.

01:09.560 --> 01:12.860
Yes. It's been a long wait.

01:25.110 --> 01:27.100
And now... To battle!

01:34.020 --> 01:47.390
Sora ni toketa hane o matoi tobitate tsubasa de

01:34.020 --> 01:40.630
Cloaked in feathers melted into the sky

01:40.630 --> 01:47.400
Take flight on wings

02:01.740 --> 02:04.910
Morokute nigai kajitsu no you ni

02:01.750 --> 02:04.920
Like fragile but bitter fruit

02:04.910 --> 02:08.120
Hito no kokoro o miryou suru no

02:04.920 --> 02:08.130
It fascinates people's hearts

02:08.120 --> 02:11.220
Togi sumasareta shiroi yubi de

02:08.130 --> 02:09.630
The shadow that manipulates

02:09.630 --> 02:11.230
With sharpened fingers gleaming white

02:11.220 --> 02:14.390
Ayatsuru kage wa chi no kaori

02:11.230 --> 02:14.400
Smells of blood

02:14.390 --> 02:27.390
Shizumi aseta kodou o yobi samasu shi no sasayaki

02:14.400 --> 02:20.840
The whisper of Death

02:20.840 --> 02:27.400
That awakens fading heartbeats

02:28.370 --> 02:34.740
Sora ni toketa hane o matoi

02:28.380 --> 02:34.750
Cloaked in feathers melted into the sky

02:34.740 --> 02:40.980
Tobitatsu no wa gin no tsubasa

02:34.750 --> 02:40.990
Silver wings take flight

02:40.980 --> 02:47.460
Fukai kaze ni tsume o tatete

02:40.990 --> 02:47.460
Become the power that tears at deep winds

02:47.460 --> 02:57.190
Kirisaku chikara to nare

02:47.460 --> 02:57.200
With poised claws

02:58.180 --> 03:01.370
Brought to you by
BiG-GuY Fansubbing

03:02.780 --> 03:07.370
Episode 11
Venus

03:07.850 --> 03:08.920
Hurry!

03:08.920 --> 03:12.320
All of the functions here will be moved
to Headquarters Laboratory.

03:12.750 --> 03:15.120
Commander, you're still here?

03:15.120 --> 03:17.330
There's something I want to test.

03:17.330 --> 03:18.190
Huh?

03:18.190 --> 03:26.330
If the nerve cells of the destroyed Gladiator are still
alive, they might turn out to be our final key.

03:26.330 --> 03:28.070
Our final key?

03:28.070 --> 03:33.010
To open that damned black box
that Nobuto left behind.

03:33.010 --> 03:36.740
The mechanical components of the Gladiators

03:36.740 --> 03:39.680
are supplemented by the implanted
nervous systems of humans.

03:39.680 --> 03:44.810
They are powered suits created with the purpose
of drawing out ever greater performance.

03:45.450 --> 03:51.430
But when the nerves of ordinary people were used,
various problems cropped up,

03:51.430 --> 03:54.060
such as in reaction time and durability.

03:54.060 --> 03:59.660
That is why it became necessary to create people
with a special nervous system.

04:04.070 --> 04:07.380
Do you understand what I'm saying, Sana?

04:07.380 --> 04:12.110
I'm trying to make this as easy
to understand as I can.

04:12.110 --> 04:14.280
Create?

04:14.280 --> 04:18.840
In other words, artificially,
using genetic engineering.

04:20.490 --> 04:22.960
You've heard of clones, haven't you?

04:22.960 --> 04:25.050
There's nothing difficult about that technology.

04:25.460 --> 04:29.660
We were created only to be
placed in those machines?

04:29.660 --> 04:31.830
Everyone except you, Sana.

04:32.070 --> 04:34.900
You have a more important role to play...

04:35.170 --> 04:37.800
because you're Venus.

04:39.710 --> 04:41.330
Venus?

04:44.810 --> 04:52.220
Vulcan, god of fire and the forge, who created the
bronze god Talos, married Venus,

04:52.220 --> 04:58.820
who then had Vulcan create the weapons
necessary for their son to conquer Rome.

04:59.460 --> 05:04.230
The genes of the Seven Children
created for the Vulcan Project

05:04.230 --> 05:08.800
will only stabilize when a Venus having the
same genes, Sana, becomes a mother,

05:08.800 --> 05:12.670
making it possible for the genes to multiply.

05:13.410 --> 05:18.210
So increased production of Gladiators
is impossible without your daughter.

05:18.210 --> 05:19.850
Is that right?

05:19.850 --> 05:24.020
I don't want to burden her with such a destiny.

05:24.020 --> 05:26.990
No... not the other children, either.

05:26.990 --> 05:29.980
And that is the reason behind the black box?

05:30.430 --> 05:33.530
You've worn a suit: I'm sure you know.

05:33.530 --> 05:40.640
The memories of fear and sorrow sealed deep within
the nervous system implanted in the suits...

05:40.640 --> 05:44.440
link up with the nerves of the pilot,
gnawing at him... and then...

05:45.070 --> 05:46.710
You know,

05:46.710 --> 05:56.610
those Gladiators can only be controlled by those
without the human emotions of fear and sorrow.

05:56.780 --> 05:59.920
In other words, we're of the same species.

05:59.920 --> 06:04.090
Me, the members of Phantom, and even Joe.

06:04.090 --> 06:05.390
He's not!

06:06.090 --> 06:07.760
Joe's not like that!

06:08.260 --> 06:10.160
What makes you say that?

06:12.600 --> 06:15.690
You've sure won her over, haven't you?

06:16.770 --> 06:24.840
In order to overcome that defect, after completing
the control device, Nobuto locked it away.

06:25.910 --> 06:31.890
So that the tragedy could not be repeated,
he hid the complex password in something...

06:31.890 --> 06:36.690
This is as far as I can get with the information
from Vice-Commander Tsurusawa.

06:36.690 --> 06:41.160
All we have to do is assign numerical values
to the notes to get the password, but...

06:41.160 --> 06:42.220
Commander!

06:42.930 --> 06:47.200
The one in Steve's Gladiator is completely useless.

06:47.200 --> 06:49.140
The other nervous system...

06:49.140 --> 06:50.870
Is alive, I hope.

06:50.870 --> 06:53.640
Necrosis has begun in some parts.

06:53.640 --> 06:56.640
That's fine. Connect it to the measurement system.

06:56.640 --> 06:57.940
Yes, sir!

06:58.610 --> 07:05.490
Tsurusawa once disclosed that Venus reacted in
something like pain to some notes on the piano.

07:05.820 --> 07:11.990
If there is a certain frequency to which this nervous
system with the same genetic makeup reacts...

07:22.470 --> 07:24.140
What about the others?

07:24.140 --> 07:26.070
What happened to the others?

07:26.070 --> 07:27.110
What others?

07:27.110 --> 07:28.740
The ones who were with me.

07:28.740 --> 07:32.480
Oh... You mean the 3rd-generation Seven Children?

07:32.480 --> 07:35.310
They're all in Phantom's Laboratory.

07:38.250 --> 07:39.180
Down!

07:43.790 --> 07:44.880
Jin!

07:50.230 --> 07:51.930
Find Venus!

07:54.440 --> 07:55.460
Is that Joe?!

07:55.670 --> 07:56.530
Attack!

08:25.730 --> 08:28.340
It's unlucky to have the
crescent moon at your back.

08:28.340 --> 08:29.800
Didn't you know?

08:29.800 --> 08:32.400
The crescent moon is called Death's Sickle.

08:52.290 --> 08:53.450
Damn!

09:02.800 --> 09:04.270
His gun's jammed!

09:04.270 --> 09:07.070
That's why I told you not to turn
your back to the crescent moon!

10:05.370 --> 10:07.360
Well, I'll be going.

10:08.270 --> 10:12.600
I'll find the quickest route to contact the others.

10:13.140 --> 10:14.540
Be careful.

10:31.730 --> 10:33.260
The laboratory?

10:33.260 --> 10:36.860
Right. I want to save them all, Joe.

10:36.860 --> 10:37.960
No.

10:39.500 --> 10:42.870
But, but he said they're all in the laboratory.

10:42.870 --> 10:45.130
They may not be alive.

10:48.040 --> 10:50.740
It's no use thinking about such things.

11:05.730 --> 11:07.090
Sagami?

11:07.090 --> 11:12.270
Even Shimousa and Kai...
It's not happening only in the Kanto area.

11:12.270 --> 11:18.070
We've received intelligence reports that rebels are
organizing in Revinus all over the country.

11:18.710 --> 11:22.840
Don't tell me word of the situation
in Satsuma has gotten out.

11:22.840 --> 11:25.650
There's no telling where a rumor starts.

11:25.650 --> 11:28.020
Actually, there is more than smoke there.

11:28.020 --> 11:32.750
It is an obvious fact that the occupation forces
in Satsuma are fighting against heavy odds.

11:32.750 --> 11:34.990
We have sent reinforcements.

11:34.990 --> 11:41.520
Once momentum is lost, investing a little more
materiel will not change the situation.

11:42.200 --> 11:46.670
Lf, by chance, Satsuma regains power
and starts to move,

11:46.670 --> 11:50.400
rebels everywhere could very well
rise up en masse.

11:50.470 --> 11:52.340
So what do you want me to do?

11:52.340 --> 11:54.240
I want you to advise the higher ups.

11:54.240 --> 11:56.480
The higher ups? To do what?

11:56.480 --> 11:59.940
Request reinforcement troops
from the Freedom States.

12:00.950 --> 12:04.490
And compromise our current
semi-isolationist policy?

12:04.490 --> 12:07.050
You want foreign troops in our country?

12:07.050 --> 12:09.360
That shouldn't surprise you.

12:09.360 --> 12:15.060
If the leader of your faction had not relied on
foreign help to oust the anti-foreigner faction,

12:15.060 --> 12:17.930
you wouldn't be in that seat today.

12:21.170 --> 12:25.140
This is also in line with the views of
the Freedom States.

12:25.140 --> 12:28.630
Surely you can have no objections, can you?

12:41.620 --> 12:42.420
Gora!

12:42.590 --> 12:44.180
Where do you think you're going?

12:44.690 --> 12:46.260
Where?

12:46.260 --> 12:48.060
Don't act innocent.

12:48.060 --> 12:51.430
You were probably waiting for Joe
to go out on patrol, right?

12:52.370 --> 12:55.960
Are you seriously thinking of going
to save your friends?

12:56.640 --> 12:59.870
Didn't Joe say they might not be alive?

12:59.870 --> 13:04.080
Even if that's true, I don't want
to leave things as they are.

13:04.080 --> 13:09.910
Just think! They're going to be put into machines!
What if it were you?

13:10.180 --> 13:12.810
I can't leave them like that.

13:15.020 --> 13:16.820
Hold on, will you?

13:16.820 --> 13:18.730
Wait, I said.

13:18.730 --> 13:21.060
Do you know the way?

13:22.000 --> 13:22.960
I'll ask.

13:22.960 --> 13:26.630
Good grief. Who do you think will tell you?

13:26.630 --> 13:28.830
That's why you're such a princess.

13:29.270 --> 13:32.110
I'll help you for three lunches.

13:32.110 --> 13:32.810
Huh?

13:32.810 --> 13:37.510
I'm saying I'll show you the way.
I'll even get us a ride.

13:37.510 --> 13:38.880
Gora!

13:41.080 --> 13:42.480
Sana!

13:58.030 --> 14:00.500
This is weird, there's nobody here.

14:00.500 --> 14:02.130
Wait here, okay?

14:15.820 --> 14:17.980
Did they move?

14:25.030 --> 14:26.720
Let go of me!

14:29.660 --> 14:31.190
Gora.

14:33.370 --> 14:36.060
I figured you'd come, Sana.

14:36.270 --> 14:39.870
Because you're such a nice girl
who thinks of her friends.

14:46.380 --> 14:47.470
Sana!

14:50.890 --> 14:52.820
Gora! Gora!

14:55.220 --> 14:58.420
J-Joe... It was Jin!

14:58.530 --> 14:59.620
Jin?!

15:27.490 --> 15:30.390
Good job, Vice-Commander Tsurusawa.

15:32.290 --> 15:35.420
Didn't you bring me Venus?

15:35.530 --> 15:38.970
There should be no reason for you
to be skulking about.

15:39.730 --> 15:47.200
I learned, not long ago, that you had
data and materials hidden here.

15:47.740 --> 15:49.800
The timing was perfect.

15:51.010 --> 15:54.180
Studying whatever is here still
wouldn't solve everything.

15:54.180 --> 15:55.720
Don't worry.

15:55.720 --> 15:59.620
We have already completed the
analysis of the black box.

16:00.150 --> 16:02.660
Without your help.

16:02.660 --> 16:03.590
What?

16:03.590 --> 16:11.160
We knew the key to extracting the data embedded
into that music lay in a certain frequency.

16:11.370 --> 16:16.400
And even that it could be obtained
by minor changes in the tuning.

16:16.400 --> 16:19.840
No one other than Sana should
be able to detect that.

16:20.340 --> 16:25.250
True, some things are difficult
to recreate in analog.

16:25.250 --> 16:27.380
However, fortunately or unfortunately,

16:27.380 --> 16:34.550
that frequency places a physical load on Venus,
as well as on those who share the same genes.

16:35.290 --> 16:43.400
With a fragment of a body bearing the same genes,
we could reverse-engineer that frequency.

16:43.400 --> 16:45.870
It was time-consuming, of course...

16:45.870 --> 16:49.430
So now, there's no reason to keep you alive.

16:49.600 --> 16:54.880
Seems you were planning to make an escape,
but we've taken that helicopter on the roof.

16:54.880 --> 16:56.880
And Venus, too.

16:56.880 --> 17:02.680
All of the keys to mass-producing
Gladiators are now in my hands.

17:04.120 --> 17:09.020
And now, you plan to give them all
to the Freedom States. Is that so?

17:09.020 --> 17:11.890
In order to turn this nation into a puppet state.

17:14.600 --> 17:17.400
Venus, Vulcan's wife...

17:17.400 --> 17:19.970
while hailed as the goddess of beauty and peace...

17:19.970 --> 17:24.560
falls in love with the warrior Achilles
and commits adultery with the war god Mars.

17:24.740 --> 17:29.380
But myths do not describe
that adultery as anything immoral.

17:29.380 --> 17:33.470
Instead they praise it as symbolizing "Pax Romana."

17:33.750 --> 17:37.770
Only when that balance is lost will calamity strike.

17:38.020 --> 17:42.350
Only when supported by military might
can peace be guaranteed.

17:42.690 --> 17:45.360
The conditions for the mass-production
of Gladiators will be set,

17:45.360 --> 17:48.660
and the armaments of the Freedom States
will be waiting in the background.

17:48.660 --> 17:52.500
There is no other nation with peace guaranteed
by such military might.

17:52.500 --> 17:58.840
All I want is to provide a steady supply of military
might that will bring true peace to this nation.

17:58.840 --> 18:00.770
That's interesting.

18:01.180 --> 18:06.310
Even someone like you will become talkative
in order to hide your true intentions.

18:07.450 --> 18:10.780
I cannot believe that that is your true intention.

18:11.050 --> 18:12.790
You realize it, don't you?

18:12.790 --> 18:17.620
The extraordinary potential of the Gladiators.

18:18.130 --> 18:22.720
I heard you intentionally disarmed
the limiter on Riki's Gladiator.

18:23.260 --> 18:27.600
And that you had him attack us,
even after he'd lost his mind.

18:27.600 --> 18:31.270
How much potential is there in the Gladiator?

18:31.970 --> 18:35.640
You did whatever you could
think of to test that out.

18:36.080 --> 18:37.630
Am I wrong?

18:39.610 --> 18:41.550
So, you've figured out that much?

18:41.550 --> 18:47.510
True, the Gladiators are not mere powered suits.
I'll give you that much.

18:49.020 --> 18:51.720
It's too bad you won't be able to hear the rest.

19:05.710 --> 19:07.900
I've been waiting for you, Joe.

19:08.640 --> 19:10.080
Who... Who's that?!

19:10.080 --> 19:11.570
Jin.

19:21.560 --> 19:23.110
Stay here.

19:23.860 --> 19:26.030
I figured you'd come here.

19:26.030 --> 19:29.520
Because you'd left the gunpowder hidden here.

19:30.100 --> 19:34.130
You were planning to use it to break through
the Logos checkpoint, weren't you?

19:34.130 --> 19:38.730
I know well how you think. It was always like that.

19:39.210 --> 19:40.440
What have you done with Sana?

19:40.440 --> 19:43.180
She's probably at the National Defense Force base.

19:43.180 --> 19:45.580
Sorry, but I don't have her.

19:45.580 --> 19:47.250
Jin, why?!

19:47.250 --> 19:48.380
Why?

19:48.380 --> 19:51.850
What? You want to know why I'm here?

19:51.850 --> 19:54.650
Or, is it something more fundamental?

19:57.020 --> 19:59.990
Like what my purpose was, to begin with...

20:03.200 --> 20:05.470
Your face tells me you want to know both.

20:05.470 --> 20:07.330
You've changed, Joe.

20:07.400 --> 20:10.390
You were never one to ask questions like that.

20:10.470 --> 20:13.940
Never mind. I'll tell you all you want to know.

20:13.940 --> 20:16.740
First, as to why I'm here...

20:16.740 --> 20:19.580
It's simple, Joe.

20:19.580 --> 20:21.880
I'm here to fight you.

20:26.950 --> 20:28.290
Fight?

20:28.290 --> 20:31.690
I'm saying that I wouldn't mind fighting Joe.

20:32.060 --> 20:34.900
You're a bad loser, Tsurusawa.

20:34.900 --> 20:37.060
You would not have seen it...

20:37.360 --> 20:40.930
But the last time, Joe showed amazing speed.

20:40.930 --> 20:44.740
You should be able to obtain some interesting data.

20:44.740 --> 20:48.740
Are you saying he'll recreate it while fighting you?

20:48.740 --> 20:51.710
Joe would not be the only one recreating it.

20:53.050 --> 20:57.180
I set a limiter breaker on my Gladiator.

20:57.180 --> 21:01.320
If conditions are right, I don't mind using it.

21:01.320 --> 21:05.450
It's up to you how you use the data that's yielded.

21:05.930 --> 21:10.860
I can't believe that you're merely following
the orders of the Freedom States.

21:11.500 --> 21:14.500
You want to learn everything about the Gladiators

21:14.500 --> 21:17.770
so that one day you can even control
the military of the Freedom States.

21:17.770 --> 21:20.470
That sounds like delusions of grandeur.

21:20.840 --> 21:25.240
But... I might enjoy keeping you company
in your delusions.

21:36.290 --> 21:39.730
Joe... Joe...

21:45.100 --> 21:47.600
Jin... you...

21:47.600 --> 21:50.900
Do you want to laugh at what you see
as a sorry plea for my life?

21:51.410 --> 21:53.940
I can't die yet.

21:53.940 --> 21:57.970
Not until I learn the limits of the Gladiators,
and make them my own.

21:58.650 --> 22:00.550
And, Joe...

22:00.550 --> 22:02.540
not until I defeat you!

22:25.170 --> 22:29.680
Nagai kioku no hate ni

22:25.170 --> 22:29.640
If at the end of our long memory

22:29.640 --> 22:35.480
Time will tear us apart

22:29.680 --> 22:35.510
Toki ga bokura o wakatsu nara

22:37.520 --> 22:44.160
If at the end of my sweet memory with you

22:37.550 --> 22:44.190
Kimi to amai kioku no hate ni

22:44.160 --> 22:50.460
You and I become one again

22:44.190 --> 22:50.500
Mata bokura hitotsu nara

22:50.460 --> 22:57.640
From a quietly stretched arm's length away

22:50.500 --> 22:57.670
Sotto te nobashita kyori kara

22:57.640 --> 23:02.340
I will search for the meaning

22:57.670 --> 23:02.380
lmi o sagasu kara

23:02.340 --> 23:08.180
Can you hear it? The words dance in midair

23:02.380 --> 23:08.220
Kikoeru? Kotoba ga chuu ni mau

23:08.180 --> 23:13.990
We shall meet when our wish is granted

23:08.220 --> 23:14.020
Kanaeta toki ni deau

23:13.990 --> 23:17.660
Leaving only their reverse behind

23:14.020 --> 23:17.690
Reverse dake nokoshite

23:17.660 --> 23:21.060
The torn words

23:17.690 --> 23:21.090
Chigireta kotoba

23:21.060 --> 23:27.190
Blurred time and light

23:21.090 --> 23:27.230
Kasureta jikan to hikari

23:29.370 --> 23:33.700
I have found them now

23:29.400 --> 23:33.740
lma, mitsuketa kara

23:35.350 --> 23:43.810
Next Episode

23:44.080 --> 23:47.420
The final episode of Innocent Venus:

23:47.780 --> 23:50.320
Episode 12
The World

23:48.320 --> 23:49.660
"The World"
